{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25218862",
      "title": "Introducing API Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 441,
      "videoOrder": 408,
      "sourceHash": "830c5c34270de96e5b6aafc6ec05d32d9742a37fbf3a5f0c816b641ae1ed8a7f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.429,
          "en": "So now we covered getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.429,
          "end": 7.17,
          "en": "and getStaticPaths and getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.17,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "and I hope it's clear what these functions do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 11.45,
          "en": "and why they exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.45,
          "end": 15.44,
          "en": "They allow us to fetch data for pre-rendering those pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.44,
          "end": 18.28,
          "en": "So that we pre-render the pages with the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.28,
          "end": 21.51,
          "en": "instead of without the data they might need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.51,
          "end": 22.73,
          "en": "Now, up to this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.73,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "we're only working with dummy data though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 28.78,
          "en": "which is not actually fetched from anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.78,
          "end": 30.74,
          "en": "Instead, we have this dummy array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.74,
          "end": 33.359,
          "en": "or in the case of the meetupId page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.359,
          "end": 35.51,
          "en": "actually hard-coded data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.51,
          "end": 37.24,
          "en": "in that return statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.24,
          "end": 40.51,
          "en": "And that's of course not realistic at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.51,
          "end": 43.89,
          "en": "Instead, we do have this Add New Meetup page here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.89,
          "end": 47.53,
          "en": "which would allow us to enter data for a new meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.53,
          "end": 50.68,
          "en": "And hence, we're now going to finish this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.68,
          "end": 52.42,
          "en": "by adding a real backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.42,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "with a real database where the data will be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.36,
          "en": "and from which we then fetch it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.36,
          "end": 62.65,
          "en": "And this then also allows me to show you the last major",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.65,
          "end": 64.98,
          "en": "NextJS feature, which is added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.98,
          "end": 67.395,
          "en": "by Next to your React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.395,
          "end": 71.89,
          "en": "NextJS makes it easy for us to build an API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.89,
          "end": 73.3,
          "en": "a backend API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.3,
          "end": 75.93,
          "en": "together with our front-end React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 77.97,
          "en": "in the same project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.97,
          "end": 81.65,
          "en": "For this, we can use another key NextJS feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.65,
          "end": 84.13,
          "en": "called API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.13,
          "end": 88.51,
          "en": "API routes are a special routes, special pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.51,
          "end": 90.26,
          "en": "if you wanna call it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.26,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "which don't return HTML code, but which are instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 97.92,
          "en": "about accepting incoming HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.92,
          "end": 100.9,
          "en": "also post patch, put delete requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.9,
          "end": 105.11,
          "en": "whatever you need with JSON data attached to them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.11,
          "end": 108.03,
          "en": "and which then might do whatever you need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 109.57,
          "en": "For example, store data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.57,
          "end": 112.96000000000001,
          "en": "in a database and then return JSON data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.96000000000001,
          "end": 115.37,
          "en": "So you could say API routes allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.37,
          "end": 117.99000000000001,
          "en": "to build your own API end points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.99000000000001,
          "end": 120.62,
          "en": "as part of this next project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.62,
          "end": 122.09,
          "en": "And they will then be served",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.09,
          "end": 125.32,
          "en": "by the same server as your next app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.32,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "Now to add API routes, you add a special folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 132.84,
          "en": "in your pages folder, and that's a folder named API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "And just as the pages folder has to be named pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.16,
          "en": "this folder has to be named API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.16,
          "end": 142.21,
          "en": "and it has to be in the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.21,
          "end": 144.57999999999998,
          "en": "Then the NextJS will pick up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.57999999999998,
          "end": 147.48,
          "en": "any JavaScript files stored in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.48,
          "end": 150.59,
          "en": "and turn those files into API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.59,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "So into end points, that can be targeted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 158.35,
          "en": "by requests and that should receive JSON and return JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.62,
          "end": 161.94,
          "en": "Now in this API folder, you can then again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.94,
          "end": 165.25,
          "en": "add JavaScript files where the file names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.25,
          "end": 169.24,
          "en": "will act as path segments in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.24,
          "end": 173.553,
          "en": "For example, a new-meetup.js file again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 176.67000000000002,
          "en": "now here in the API folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.67000000000002,
          "end": 179.72,
          "en": "Now, in those JavaScript files here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.72,
          "end": 183.67,
          "en": "you then don't create a React component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.67,
          "end": 186.01,
          "en": "These API routes are not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.01,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "about defining, rendering or returning React components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 192.5,
          "en": "Instead in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.5,
          "end": 196.87,
          "en": "we will define functions which contains server-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.87,
          "end": 200.24,
          "en": "because API routes will only run on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.24,
          "end": 201.86,
          "en": "never on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.86,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "Decoding them will never be exposed to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 207.46,
          "en": "So we can also use credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.46,
          "end": 211.04,
          "en": "in API routes without compromising them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.04,
          "end": 214.3,
          "en": "And those functions are then simply triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.3,
          "end": 217.54,
          "en": "whenever a request is sent to this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.54,
          "end": 221.53,
          "en": "so to /api/new-meetup here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.53,
          "end": 225.2,
          "en": "This would be the URL of this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.2,
          "end": 227.84,
          "en": "and if a request is sent to this URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.84,
          "end": 229.51,
          "en": "it will trigger the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 229.51,
          "end": 231.653,
          "en": "which we have to define in this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.53,
          "end": 234.67000000000002,
          "en": "Now often these function named handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.67000000000002,
          "end": 236.14,
          "en": "but the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.14,
          "end": 239.07999999999998,
          "en": "the important thing is that it's exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.07999999999998,
          "end": 242.72,
          "en": "So we export this handler function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.72,
          "end": 245.41,
          "en": "and this function will receive a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.41,
          "end": 247.25,
          "en": "and a response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 247.25,
          "end": 251.64,
          "en": "You might notice from node.js and express.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 251.64,
          "end": 254.16,
          "en": "The request object contains data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 255.99,
          "en": "about the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 255.99,
          "end": 258.01,
          "en": "The response object will be needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.01,
          "end": 260.253,
          "en": "for sending back a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.09,
          "end": 263.01,
          "en": "Now, from that request object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 263.01,
          "end": 266.65,
          "en": "we can get things like the headers or the request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.65,
          "end": 271.543,
          "en": "and also the request method, route a method property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.7,
          "end": 276.42,
          "en": "This allows us to find out which kind of request was sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 276.42,
          "end": 277.6,
          "en": "And we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.6,
          "end": 281.73,
          "en": "check if we are receiving having a post request here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "So if the request method is POST,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 287.43,
          "en": "and we only execute the code in this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.43,
          "end": 290.62,
          "en": "if it is a incoming post request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.62,
          "end": 294.36,
          "en": "For other kinds of requests, we don't do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.36,
          "end": 297.44,
          "en": "So that would ensure that only post requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.44,
          "end": 301.653,
          "en": "to this route would actually trigger this code in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.87,
          "end": 307.87,
          "en": "Then here, we can get our data by accessing req.body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.04,
          "end": 310.56,
          "en": "The body field is another built-in field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.56,
          "end": 313.35,
          "en": "which contains the body of the incoming request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 313.35,
          "end": 315.673,
          "en": "the data of the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.77,
          "end": 319.32,
          "en": "And then we can do whatever we need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 319.32,
          "end": 321.19,
          "en": "Now this year will be the end point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 321.19,
          "end": 323.64,
          "en": "for creating a new meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 323.64,
          "end": 327.94,
          "en": "And therefore it's probably fair to expect that this data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 327.94,
          "end": 332.14,
          "en": "which we get contains a title, a meetup image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.14,
          "end": 335.22,
          "en": "an address and a description field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 335.22,
          "end": 339.75,
          "en": "After all, it's our page, our project, and our API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 339.75,
          "end": 342.46,
          "en": "So we can expect whichever data we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 342.46,
          "end": 344.72,
          "en": "We will then just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 344.72,
          "end": 348.64,
          "en": "that we send the correct data when we do send a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 348.64,
          "end": 350.86,
          "en": "to this API route later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 350.86,
          "end": 353.17,
          "en": "But for the moment I do indeed expect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 353.17,
          "end": 356.93,
          "en": "that we get some data out of this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 356.93,
          "end": 358.5,
          "en": "so out of this request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 358.5,
          "end": 360.92,
          "en": "and I'll use object de-structuring here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.92,
          "end": 363.74,
          "en": "and I expect to get a title, a image field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.74,
          "end": 366.87,
          "en": "an address field and a description field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 366.87,
          "end": 369.91,
          "en": "So these are the four fields which I expect to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 369.91,
          "end": 373.02,
          "en": "on the incoming request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 373.02,
          "end": 377.34,
          "en": "And then we can store them in a database, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 377.34,
          "end": 379.24,
          "en": "and that's what we're going to do now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
